--- body ---
## Intent (author decisions, 2026-10-15)
`scripts/zotero.py` becomes local-only and stateless:

- Remove every Zotero Web API path (item reads and writes, file upload,
  enrichment writes), the API keys and their credential plumbing, the
  library index cache and its sync subcommand, and the injection record kept
  between runs. No local index, no cache, no record.
- Reads: `zotero.sqlite` opened read-only on every call; dedup and matching
  run against it.
- Creating items with PDFs goes through the Zotero desktop connector
  (`127.0.0.1:23119/connector/`). Zotero must be running; fail loudly when the
  connector does not answer. Never write `zotero.sqlite`.
- `enrich` and `reconcile --apply` cannot edit existing items: they report
  the suggested edits (item key, field, old → new) for the author.
- Ticket 1111 is superseded; what still applies is kept and 1111 closes in
  the same PR.
- Skill, references, `docs/zotero-integration.md`, `rules/zotero.md` and
  `README.md` carry no Web API, key or index-cache instruction. The
  "Periodic sync + purge" section of `rules/zotero.md` belongs to ticket 1112.

## Original context
2026-10-15, host doudou: `python3 scripts/zotero.py reconcile .` in report mode
on the harness, with a library index cache older than 24 h (4.7 MB, written
2026-10-14 15:21), was killed by `timeout 300` with no report. The time went
into the Web API rebuild of that cache. Removing the cache removes the cost: a
full read of the local library takes about 0.4 s (7,672 works, 9,451
attachments, measured on doudou 2026-10-15).

## Exit criteria
- [ ] No Web API call, key, index cache or injection record remains live in
      scripts/, skills/, rules/, docs/ or README.md
- [ ] Reads open zotero.sqlite read-only per call; a locked database falls
      back to the immutable snapshot and every output names its read mode
- [ ] `inject` creates items and PDFs through the desktop connector and
      fails loudly when Zotero is not running; tests use a local stub
- [ ] `enrich`, `attach` and `reconcile --apply` report edits to existing
      items instead of writing them
- [ ] `make check` passes
